$ Shallow-water propagation over a submerged bar with DCTA triads that also
$ act between waves from different directions (NONC), on a sector
$
$ The same deck as triad_dcta_nonc.swn, with the same 36 directions of 10
$ degrees given as a sector from -175 to 175 degrees and not as a full
$ circle. On a sector SWDNCTA looks up the third direction for every pair
$ of directions, as upstream does; on the full circle the fork works it out
$ once for every angle between two directions. The two decks therefore
$ run the same physics along the two routes, and their spectra should
$ agree closely. They are not equal: a sector has two ends, so a third
$ direction that falls between 175 and 185 degrees is left out, and energy
$ does not turn from one end to the other.
$
PROJECT 'TRIADNOS' '001'
SET CARTESIAN
MODE STATIONARY ONEDIMENSIONAL
COORDINATES CARTESIAN

CGRID REGULAR 0.0 0.0 0.0 30.0 0.0 300 0 &
      SECTOR -175.0 175.0 35 0.10 2.0 31
INPGRID BOTTOM REGULAR 0.0 0.0 0.0 30 0 1.0 1.0
READINP BOTTOM 1.0 'bottom.bot' 1 0 FREE

BOUND SHAPESPEC JONSWAP 3.3 PEAK DSPR DEGREES
BOUNDSPEC SIDE WEST CONSTANT PAR 0.06 2.0 0.0 10.0

GEN3 WESTH
OFF WINDGROWTH
OFF WCAPPING
OFF QUADRUPLET
TRIAD DCTA NONC

POINTS 'GAUGES' 2.0 0.0 10.0 0.0 15.0 0.0 18.0 0.0 &
         25.0 0.0 30.0 0.0
TABLE 'GAUGES' HEADER 'triad_dcta_nonc_sector.tbl' XP DEPTH HSIGN TM01 RTP REDTRIAD REDQUAD
SPECOUT 'GAUGES' SPEC1D ABS 'triad_dcta_nonc_sector.spc'
TEST 1 0 POINTS XY 15.0 0.0 S1D 'triad_dcta_nonc_sector_sources.spc'

COMPUTE
STOP
